{"type":"message","id":"d467653b","parentId":"1dc2c4e1","timestamp":"2026-06-23T00:12:58.685Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_tR5FHUmSGxZqP7ISQskU5178","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nquery_price.py - 查询实时价格（直接读 crypto_signal_monitor 的状态文件）\n\n用法：\n    python3 query_price.py                # 查询所有 7 个币种 → stdout\n    python3 query_price.py BTC            # 查询单个 → stdout\n    python3 query_price.py BTC ETH        # 查询多个 → stdout\n    python3 query_price.py --push         # 所有币种推送卡片到飞书群\n    python3 query_price.py BTC --push     # 单币种推送卡片到飞书群\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\nSCRIPT_DIR = Path(__file__).parent\nSTATE_FILE = SCRIPT_DIR / \"crypto_state.json\"\nSTALE_SECONDS = 60\n\nEMOJI = {\n    \"BTC\": \"👑\", \"ETH\": \"💎\", \"SOL\": \"⚡\",\n    \"BNB\": \"🔶\", \"DOT\": \"🌐\", \"LINK\": \"🔗\", \"XRP\": \"🪙\",\n}\n\n\ndef load_state():\n    if not STATE_FILE.exists():\n        print(\"[ERROR] crypto_state.json 不存在 —— 监控未启动\")\n        sys.exit(2)\n    try:\n        return json.loads(STATE_FILE.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"[ERROR] 读取失败: {e}\")\n        sys.exit(3)\n\n\ndef calc_age(state):\n    try:\n        ts = datetime.fromisoformat(state.get(\"last_update\", \"\"))\n        return (datetime.now() - ts).total_seconds()\n    except Exception:\n        return 99999\n\n\ndef main():\n    args = sys.argv[1:]\n    push_card_mode = \"--push\" in args\n    if push_card_mode:\n        args.remove(\"--push\")\n\n    state = load_state()\n    age = calc_age(state)\n    prices = state.get(\"prices\", {})\n\n    if age > STALE_SECONDS:\n        print(f\"[STALE] 数据已过期 {int(age)} 秒（最后更新: {state.get('last_update')}）\")\n        print(\"[ACTION] 执行 `kj` 重启监控系统\")\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    requested = [s.upper() for s in args] or list(prices.keys())\n\n    if push_card_mode:\n        from feishu_helper import push_card, md, hr, note, kv_block\n        # 找到的币种和缺失的币种\n        found = [(sym, prices.get(sym)) for sym in requested if prices.get(sym) is not None]\n        missing = [sym for sym in requested if prices.get(sym) is None]\n        \n        elements = []\n        if not found:\n            elements.append(md(\"⚠️ **未找到任何匹配币种**\"))\n        else:\n            # 用 kv_block 两列网格布局，最美观\n            items = []\n            for sym, px in found:\n                emo = EMOJI.get(sym, \"🟣\")\n                items.append((f\"{emo} {sym}\", f\"`${px:,g}`\"))\n            # kv_block 一次最多放偶数个比较好看，不够补\"—\"\n            if len(items) % 2 == 1:\n                items.append((\"\", \"\"))\n            elements.append(kv_block(items))\n        \n        if missing:\n            elements.append(hr())\n            elements.append(md(\n                f\"<font color='grey'>未在监控列表：{', '.join(missing)}</font>\"\n            ))\n        \n        elements.append(note(\n            f\"📡 Binance WSS · 更新于 {int(age)} 秒前 · \"\n            f\"{datetime.now().strftime('%H:%M:%S')}\"\n        ))\n        ok = push_card(\"👑 实时行情\", elements, template=\"blue\")\n        print(\"[PUSH] OK\" if ok else \"[PUSH] FAILED\")\n        return\n\n    print(f\"[OK] 实时价格 (更新于 {int(age)} 秒前)\")\n    for sym in requested:\n        px = prices.get(sym)\n        if px is None:\n            print(f\"  {sym}: 不在监控列表\")\n        else:\n            print(f\"  {EMOJI.get(sym, ' ')} {sym}: {px} USDT\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1782173578667}}
{"type":"message","id":"fbf7e715","parentId":"d467653b","timestamp":"2026-06-23T00:13:01.264Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see the issue. The script prints `[PUSH] OK` twice. Let me look at the `feishu_helper.push_card` function. But more importantly, the user says they didn't see anything and got \"未找到任何匹配币种\" - this is the message when `found` is empty, meaning no prices were found for the requested coins.\n\nWait, the second `[PUSH] OK` might be from something else. Let me check if there's a wrapper or something.\n\nActually, let me read the feishu_helper to understand the push_card function.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_pduovEV6MBuZoT3GOoES2277","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && grep -n 'def push_card\\|print.*PUSH\\|PUSH' feishu_helper.py | head -20","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":996,"output":340,"cacheRead":22528,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23864,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1782173578688}}
{"type":"message","id":"f07a4313","parentId":"fbf7e715","timestamp":"2026-06-23T00:13:01.366Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_pduovEV6MBuZoT3GOoES2277","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"64:def push_card(title: str, elements: list, template: str = \"blue\") -> bool:\n104:            print(f\"[PUSH] OK -> chat_id={chat_id}\")\n118:                    print(f\"[PUSH] OK -> chat_id={chat_id}\")\n120:        print(f\"[PUSH] FAILED chat_id={chat_id} reason={data}\")\n122:        print(f\"[PUSH] FAILED chat_id={chat_id} exception={e}\")"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":79,"aggregated":"64:def push_card(title: str, elements: list, template: str = \"blue\") -> bool:\n104:            print(f\"[PUSH] OK -> chat_id={chat_id}\")\n118:                    print(f\"[PUSH] OK -> chat_id={chat_id}\")\n120:        print(f\"[PUSH] FAILED chat_id={chat_id} reason={data}\")\n122:        print(f\"[PUSH] FAILED chat_id={chat_id} exception={e}\")","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1782173581355}}
{"type":"message","id":"c3ad732b","parentId":"f07a4313","timestamp":"2026-06-23T00:13:06.548Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So there are two `print(\"[PUSH] OK\")` lines in the feishu_helper.py. Let me look at the context around those lines to understand why it prints twice.\n\nBut more importantly, the user said they got \"未找到任何匹配币种\" - this means the script ran and found no prices. This could happen if:\n1. The crypto_state.json had no prices for the coins\n2. The state data was empty\n\nWait, the health check showed `crypto_state 实时刷新 8秒前更新, 7 个币种` - so the data was there.\n\nHmm, could it be that when I ran `--all` the first time, `--all` was not recognized as a coin and was treated as a coin symbol? And the second run with just `--push` pushed the card but the user couldn't see it because... maybe the card just appeared and they just need to scroll up?\n\nActually, let me re-read the user's message: \"没有看见，未找到任何匹配币种\"\n\nThis is exactly the error message from the script: `⚠️ **未找到任何匹配币种**`. This means the card WAS pushed, but it contained the error message. So the user DID receive a card saying no coins were found.\n\nBut why? Let me think... The user replied to an interactive card saying \"为什么只有btc的其他的呢\". Maybe the first `query_price.py --all --push` run failed because `--all` was treated as a coin symbol and not found. Then the second run with `query_price.py --push` should have worked correctly...\n\nWait, but the second run also returned `[PUSH] OK` - that means success. The card should have all coins.\n\nActually, let me look at the `[PUSH] OK` printed twice issue. Maybe the second one is from a different path. Let me check the feishu_helper more carefully.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_LHOL3FB5OxwgGToPwGLg8735","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/feishu_helper.py","offset":60,"limit":70}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":174,"output":897,"cacheRead":23680,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":24751,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1782173581369}}
{"type":"message","id":"85f410a3","parentId":"c3ad732b","timestamp":"2026-06-23T00:13:06.600Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_LHOL3FB5OxwgGToPwGLg8735","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"        print(f\"[helper] 获取飞书 token 失败: {e}\")\n    return None\n\n\ndef push_card(title: str, elements: list, template: str = \"blue\") -> bool:\n    \"\"\"推送飞书卡片消息到目标群\"\"\"\n    chat_id = _load_chat_id()\n    if not chat_id:\n        print(\"[helper] 找不到 feishu_chat_id，无法发送\")\n        return False\n\n    token = get_token()\n    if not token:\n        print(\"[helper] 飞书 token 获取失败\")\n        return False\n\n    card_content = {\n        \"config\": {\"wide_screen_mode\": True},\n        \"header\": {\n            \"template\": template,\n            \"title\": {\"tag\": \"plain_text\", \"content\": title},\n        },\n        \"elements\": elements,\n    }\n    url = \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/im/v1/messages?receive_id_type=chat_id\"\n    headers = {\n        \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\",\n        \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n    }\n    payload = {\n        \"receive_id\": chat_id,\n        \"msg_type\": \"interactive\",\n        \"content\": json.dumps(card_content, ensure_ascii=False),\n    }\n    try:\n        r = requests.post(\n            url,\n            headers=headers,\n            data=json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False),\n            timeout=10,\n            proxies=None,\n        )\n        data = r.json()\n        if data.get(\"code\") == 0:\n            print(f\"[PUSH] OK -> chat_id={chat_id}\")\n            return True\n        if data.get(\"code\") == 99991663:\n            token = get_token(force_refresh=True)\n            if token:\n                headers[\"Authorization\"] = f\"Bearer {token}\"\n                r = requests.post(\n                    url,\n                    headers=headers,\n                    data=json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False),\n                    timeout=10,\n                    proxies=None,\n                )\n                if r.json().get(\"code\") == 0:\n                    print(f\"[PUSH] OK -> chat_id={chat_id}\")\n                    return True\n        print(f\"[PUSH] FAILED chat_id={chat_id} reason={data}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"[PUSH] FAILED chat_id={chat_id} exception={e}\")\n    return False\n\n\ndef md(text: str) -> dict:\n    return {\"tag\": \"div\", \"text\": {\"tag\": \"lark_md\", \"content\": text}}\n\n\n\n[52 more lines in file. Use offset=130 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1782173586585}}
{"type":"message","id":"e5c9bebf","parentId":"85f410a3","timestamp":"2026-06-23T00:13:16.406Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so `[PUSH] OK` printed twice means two separate push_card calls succeeded. The first was probably from the `--all --push` which treated `--all` as a coin (not found), pushed a card saying \"未找到任何匹配币种\". The second was from `--push` which should have pushed all coins correctly.\n\nBut the user says they didn't see it. Let me re-check - maybe the second `[PUSH] OK` isn't from query_price.py at all. Let me look at the output again:\n\nFirst run (`query_price.py --all --push`):\n```\n[PUSH] OK -> chat_id=oc_a04a61675c784d76c345fde6501e8f49\n[PUSH] OK\n```\n\nSecond run (`query_price.py --push`):\n```\n[PUSH] OK -> chat_id=oc_a04a61675c784d76c345fde6501e8f49\n[PUSH] OK\n```\n\nWait, both show `[PUSH] OK` twice. The first line has the chat_id, the second doesn't. Let me look at what could cause this...\n\nActually wait, maybe there's a retry happening. If the first attempt gets code 99991663 (token expired), it retries with a new token, and both succeed in printing. But that would mean both attempts succeeded...\n\nActually no, looking at the code:\n- Line 104: prints if code == 0\n- Line 118: prints if retry also returns code == 0\n\nSo both lines can print. That's not a bug, just verbose logging. Both mean the push succeeded.\n\nNow the real question: why did the user see \"未找到任何匹配币种\"? \n\nThe first run `query_price.py --all --push` treated `--all` as a coin symbol. The `requested` list became `['--ALL']` (after removing `--push`), and since `--ALL` is not in prices, `found` was empty, resulting in the error card.\n\nThe second run `query_price.py --push` should have been correct - no args left after removing `--push`, so `requested` = all prices keys. This should have pushed all coins.\n\nBut the user says they didn't see it and got \"未找到任何匹配币种\". Maybe the second run ALSO had issues. Or maybe both `[PUSH] OK` in the second run correspond to: the first push was the old \"未找到\" card from a previous script invocation, and the second was the correct one?\n\nActually wait, I think the issue might be simpler. Let me look at the `[PUSH] OK` without chat_id. The first `[PUSH] OK` in `feishu_helper.py` is at line 104 with chat_id. The second at line 118 also with chat_id.\n\nLet me re-read more carefully:\n- Line 104: `print(f\"[PUSH] OK -> chat_id={chat_id}\")`\n- Line 118: `print(f\"[PUSH] OK -> chat_id={chat_id}\")`\n\nBoth should include chat_id! But my output shows:\n```\n[PUSH] OK -> chat_id=oc_a04a61675c784d76c345fde6501e8f49\n[PUSH] OK\n```\n\nThe second line doesn't have chat_id. That's odd. Unless `chat_id` somehow changes between the two prints? No...\n\nHmm, actually wait - `[PUSH] OK` without chat_id exists in the query_price.py script itself! At the end of main():\n```python\nok = push_card(...)\nprint(\"[PUSH] OK\" if ok else \"[PUSH] FAILED\")\n```\n\nSo:\n1. feishu_helper.push_card() prints `[PUSH] OK -> chat_id=...` (line 104 or 118)\n2. query_price.py then prints `[PUSH] OK` (based on return value)\n\nThis is just double logging. Both mean success.\n\nSo the second run (`query_price.py --push`) DID push the all-coins card successfully. The user might have:\n- Seen the first error card from the `--all` attempt\n- Not noticed the second correct card\n- Or the second card got mixed up in the chat\n\nI should just tell the user that the all-coins card was pushed successfully. They should scroll up and look for the \"👑 实时行情\" card.\n\nActually, let me just try pushing once more to make sure. But also, maybe I should look at what's actually in the crypto_state.json to verify data is there.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_kTC8wUplgohxbUmZLs183214","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_state.json | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print('last_update:', d.get('last_update')); print('prices:', json.dumps(d.get('prices',{}), indent=2))\"","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":595,"output":2095,"cacheRead":24320,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":27010,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1782173586604}}
